Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: Stop splitting degenerate overlapping bezier control triangles.

d2d_geometry_resolve_beziers() splits the larger of two overlapping bezier
control triangles until they no longer overlap, without a lower bound. For
nearly coincident curves (FenixDisplay produces them in PFD/ND glyph and
symbol outlines) float rounding can keep the halves overlapping forever, so
ID2D1GeometrySink::Close() never returns and the display thread hangs at
100% CPU. Stop once both triangles have degenerated below 1e-5 (or are NaN)
and treat the pair as not overlapping.
---
--- a/dlls/d2d1/geometry.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/geometry.c
@@ -3419,7 +3419,15 @@
         {
             while (d2d_geometry_check_bezier_overlap(geometry, &idx_p, &idx_q))
             {
-                if (fabsf(d2d_geometry_bezier_ccw(geometry, &idx_q)) > fabsf(d2d_geometry_bezier_ccw(geometry, &idx_p)))
+                float area_p = fabsf(d2d_geometry_bezier_ccw(geometry, &idx_p));
+                float area_q = fabsf(d2d_geometry_bezier_ccw(geometry, &idx_q));
+
+                /* Each split roughly halves a control triangle. For nearly
+                 * coincident curves rounding can keep the triangles overlapping
+                 * forever, so stop once both have degenerated (or are NaN). */
+                if (!(area_p >= 1e-5f || area_q >= 1e-5f))
+                    break;
+                if (area_q > area_p)
                 {
                     if (!d2d_geometry_split_bezier(geometry, &idx_q))
                         return E_OUTOFMEMORY;
